From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Date: Fri Aug 29 16:25:00 2026 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] spi-flash: suppress 16MiB warning for 4-byte-addressed chips

The Ingenic SFC NOR driver accesses chips larger than 16MiB natively by
entering 4-byte address mode (EN4B/EX4B) and setting addr_size to 4 in
the flash descriptor. The generic probe warning assumes the only way
past 16MiB is the bank/extension address register behind
CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_BAR, so it wrongly tells the user the upper half of a
32MiB chip is unreachable.

Only warn when the descriptor does not already advertise 4-byte
addressing; chips probed through the Ingenic driver with addr_size == 4
skip the warning.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
 drivers/mtd/spi/spi_flash.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/spi/spi_flash.c b/drivers/mtd/spi/spi_flash.c
--- a/drivers/mtd/spi/spi_flash.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/spi/spi_flash.c
@@ -646,7 +646,7 @@
 		printf(", mapped at %p", flash->memory_map);
 	puts("\n");
 #ifndef CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_BAR
-	if (flash->size > SPI_FLASH_16MB_BOUN) {
+	if (flash->size > SPI_FLASH_16MB_BOUN && flash->addr_size < 4) {
 		puts("SF:    Warning! Only lower 16MiB are accessible.");
 		puts(" Add #define CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_BAR for full access.\n");
 	}
